From 87b3abac413f4e016ae8a55c838b01f597d03bff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Takuro Ashie <ashie@clear-code.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:13:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] ozone/wayland: add V4L2 no-scale overlay path

Add a V4L2NoScaleOverlay feature for RZ/G2L Wayland/Westonl deployments
where V4L2 decoded NV12 dmabufs can be promoted to a KMS plane only
when the video is displayed without scaling or cropping.

The feature keeps no-scale NV12 overlay candidates alive during Viz
prioritization, treats invalid NV12 dmabuf modifiers as LINEAR for
import, promotes the NV12 Wayland overlay z-order, and makes Wayland
overlay delegation active when V4L2NoScaleOverlay is enabled. Scaled or
cropped NV12 candidates are rejected so they fall back to GPU
composition instead of failing Weston atomic tests.

The debug logs are rate-limited and gated by V4L2NoScaleOverlay.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [RZ/G2L-specific V4L2/Weston overlay workaround]
